# Ratchet context (generated; refreshed before every turn)

## Objective
- Metric: `http_req_duration.p95` (minimize). A candidate must beat the current best by more than 3.0% and more than the benchmark noise floor.
- Baseline: 20
- Current ratchet best: 12.5 (commit 11111111); improvement so far 37.5%

## Limits
- Time remaining: 58m
- Budget remaining: $15.50 of $20.00
- Turn: 3; candidates submitted: 2

## History of your candidates
| # | commit | verdict | best after | notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | abcdef12 | blocked | 20 | touches protected path bench/run.sh |
| 2 | 11111111 | verified | 12.5 | - |

## Rules
- Protected paths (a candidate touching them is blocked): `ratchet.yaml`, `bench/**`, and lockfiles / install config (`pnpm-lock.yaml`, `package-lock.json`, `npm-shrinkwrap.json`, `yarn.lock`, `bun.lock`, `bun.lockb`, `.npmrc`, `.yarnrc`, `.yarnrc.yml`, `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, `.pnpmfile.cjs`) at any depth
- Guardrails checked on every candidate: `pnpm test` must pass; `error_rate` < 0.001
- Dependencies are fixed: the trusted benchmark has no network and installs from the lockfile of the base ref. A candidate that changes the lockfile (pnpm-lock.yaml, package-lock.json) is blocked, so do not add or upgrade packages.
- The trusted benchmark runs on pinned hardware and a hidden trace; your own measurements only guide you.

## How to submit
- Commit one idea per commit. The runner submits your newest commit (or commits a dirty tree for you) with the trailer `Ratchet-Candidate: true`; do not push yourself.
- After each verdict you are resumed with the result. When another agent moves the ratchet best, the runner rebases your branch onto it (conflicts resolved in favour of the best).
- To abandon rejected work and start from the last accepted tree: `git reset --hard refs/ratchet/accepted`.
